Bugfix: Make the app menu toggle a button of its own

The app menu toggle of the signed-in layout was an <a href="#"> that wrapped
both the burger and the page heading. HTML does not allow interactive content
inside an anchor, so the accessible name of the toggle merged the burger label
with the heading. The toggle also sat behind the logo in the document, which
put the focus on the centred logo before the control at the left edge of the
header, and the burger itself measured 14 by 10 pixels.

The wrapper is a plain div now, and the toggle is a button of 29 by 45 pixels
that carries its own translated name. The block moved in front of the logo, so
the tab order follows the header from left to right. The search box and the
user menu share a flex container, which binds their display order to the markup
instead of to their float direction. The skip link shows its focus below the
header instead of over the app title. No element in the header moved.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.3, SC 2.5.8, SC 4.1.2
